  "id": "2026-09-16-pagination-view-owned-implementation",
  "scope": "pagination",
  "kind": "review",
  "date": "2026-09-16",
  "question": "Which document and measurement contracts determine pages, and which layout authority can be removed or reused?",
  "model": "GPT-6 / Codex",
  "method": "best-api-review/history-v2; Redesign from First Principles; Task S0-S6 execution; Plite Plan; Verify Plate; production cost and browser proof",
  "trigger": "The user authorized direct execution of the accepted pagination plan and required a final harsh completeness pass.",
  "requirements": [
    "Keep canonical content, history and collaboration in the editor while one mounted PagedEditable owns live measurement, page surfaces, projection, omission and retirement.",
    "Expose one-shot headless measurePages and exact-host committed layout reads; derived page boundaries never become document authority.",
    "Represent fragmentation as text, one atomic owner or every direct element child, derive source paths internally and preserve complete source content.",
    "Delete the public live controller, page-break persistence, generic geometry/path lookup, box/split vocabulary, timing controls and caller decoration publication without compatibility aliases.",
    "Keep Plate as an exact facade, adopt every app/docs/package consumer and prove native editing, omission, package boundaries, packed artifacts, cost and doctrine."
  ],
  "evidenceReuse": "Reused the accepted ownership laws and six frozen design probes while their requirements held. Rechecked every declared live owner and consumer after adoption, added a production-source five-cohort receipt, reran focused package/type/lint/browser proof, packed-release and registry gates, and recorded unrelated aggregate interruptions separately.",
  "summary": "Pursue is implemented and verified for pagination. PagedEditable owns live layout and explicit page omission; measurePages is the one-shot headless operation; exact-host hooks expose only committed layout and current-element fragments. Fragmentation is text, atomic or direct children with paths derived internally. False page-break authority, the live controller, public boxes/splits/geometry readers, caller projection publication and timing controls are deleted across Plite, Plate, the app, docs and release contracts.",
  "verdict": "pursue",
  "previous": "2026-09-15-pagination-render-page-closure",
  "relation": "reaffirms",
  "alternatives": [
    "Keep the public live layout controller and move only helper calls: rejected because applications would still assemble lifetime, projection and decoration publication for one mounted view.",
    "Persist page-break snapshots as editor authority: rejected because the old data neither reconstructed intra-block breaks nor controlled composition and introduced document writes for derived geometry.",
    "Route page layouts through the generic block virtualizer or a pagination plugin/store: rejected because pagination already owns page coordinates and the mounted view lifetime.",
    "Selected target: one view-owned paged component, one-shot headless measurement, exact-host reads and internally derived text/atomic/direct-child fragmentation."
  ],
  "proofLimits": "Focused pagination proof is complete: 37 package tests, 101 assertions; a 41,693-assertion frozen production cost packet; four pagination and six query-control Chromium cases; packed declarations/SSR/DCE/optional-peer proof; registry and doctrine closure. No physical-device IME, native Find UI, print preview, accessibility traversal, cross-machine typography or publication is claimed. The root strict gate stopped on an unrelated concurrent history README assertion after 96 typecheck tasks, and a later full Chromium run was invalidated by a concurrent slash-test write; the plan preserves those limits without weakening pagination acceptance.",
